# Test Report Rules

Rules for the Anan Agent test results report and all related charts, timelines, improvement tracking, and testing infrastructure.

---

## 1. Report Structure (Required Sections, in Order)

The report must include these sections in this order:

| Order | Section | Purpose |
|-------|---------|---------|
| 1 | **Header** | Title, subtitle, generated timestamp, model, test count |
| 2 | **Methodology** | Test environment, sample size (N), pass criteria, reproducibility commands |
| 3 | **Main Highlight** | Final pass % with Wilson 95% CI, summary line |
| 4 | **Stats Row** | Total, Passed, Failed + category stats (Formatting, Images, Search, Memory, IQ) with 95% CI |
| 5 | **Session Timeline** | Chronological improvement milestones (see Timeline rules) |
| 6 | **Charts** | Progress, Category, Response Times, Distribution, Radar, Heatmap |
| 7 | **Models Evaluated** | Model cards with status (BEST/WORKS/ISSUES/FAILED) |
| 8 | **Per-Test Table** | Test ID, Category, Description, Pass/Fail, Duration, Failure Reason |
| 9 | **All Tests Grid** | Visual test cards (pass/fail icons) |
| 10 | **Sample Output** | Example input/output from agent |
| 11 | **Files Modified** | File, Change, Status |
| 12 | **Next Steps** | Priority, Task, Description |
| 13 | **Footer** | Session date, deployment, model, export hint |

---

## 2. Test Suite Conventions

### Focused Suite (tests/focused-test.cjs)

- **20 tests** across 5 categories:
  - Formatting (FMT-001..FMT-005): 5 tests
  - Images (IMG-001..IMG-004): 4 tests
  - Search (SRCH-001..SRCH-004): 4 tests
  - Memory (MEM-001..MEM-004): 4 tests
  - IQ (IQ-001..IQ-003): 3 tests
- **Test ID format**: `{CAT}-{NNN}` (e.g., FMT-001, SRCH-004).
- **Run**: `node tests/focused-test.cjs <thread_id> [--json]`
- **JSON output** (--json): `{ timestamp, threadId, total, passCount, passRate, results, durations }`

### Column Tests (scripts/run-column-tests.ts)

- **~14 scenarios** from `convex/agents/anan/testing/column_tests.ts`: A1–A3, B1–B3, F1–F2, R1–R5, G1–G2.
- **Intents**: search, another, more_details, handoff, objection.
- **API**: POST `/api/test/column` with `{ userId?, channel?, testCaseIds? }`
- **Run**: `bun run scripts/run-column-tests.ts`

### Report Data Source

- The HTML report is primarily driven by **focused suite** results.
- When using `generate-test-report.ts`, it reads focused-test JSON (stdin or `--input`) and updates the report template.

